Thanks for reaching out,
my suggestion would be, that before real funds enter, prioritise three additional acceptance runs:
a cross-LSP payment interrupted after the recipient’s credit is committed but before upstream completion, followed by a process crash and retry of the same invoice;
a partition carried through forced closure, testing both preimage claims and timeout refunds;
a wallet exit with the LSP, gateway and operator watchtower all unavailable, using only recovery material already held by the user and an independent CKB endpoint.
